    3. Pick a bar color from {blue, green, grey, magenta, orange, maroon} (not red/yellow/black)
    4. Generate two contiguous bar segments within [0, W-1] with different lengths (each 1 to W), ensuring overlap >= 1 column
    5. Assign the longer bar to top or bottom randomly; place shorter on the other edge row
    6. Fill the rest with black
    7. Verify: fill region (overlap cols, rows between longer-bar edge and separator) is all black -- guaranteed by construction
```
